---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="colophon · field notes"
  description="How this site is made: Astro, Tailwind, a field-notes design system, and no JavaScript where CSS will do."
  crumb="colophon"
>
  <main class="doc">
    <section class="hero">
      <span class="label kicker">site · colophon</span>
      <h1>Colophon</h1>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule rule--hard" />

    <p>This site is a static build: Astro with Tailwind, set in Source Serif 4
    and IBM Plex Mono. The visual language is a field notebook — paper ground,
    ink, hairlines, and vermillion stamps for status marks.</p>

    <p>The ruler along the bottom edge measures your progress down the page.
    It is drawn and driven entirely in CSS — no JavaScript moves it. The dot
    marks on the right are the only script on most pages: a small observer
    that notes which section you are reading.</p>

    <p>Status stamps mean what they say. <span class="stamp">concept</span>
    means no code yet; <span class="stamp stamp--live">partially live</span>
    means some of it runs and some of it does not. The absence of a claim is
    itself a record.</p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { margin: 0 0 var(--sp-2); }
  .hero .kicker { display: block; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h1);
    line-height: 1.02;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
</style>
